    "overview": "Schneider’s skink (Eumeces schneiderii) is a scincid lizard. Tarkhnishvili et al. 2026 list it as biologically confirmed: the species occurs in West Asia and North Africa; subspecies E. s. princeps is the Caucasus/Iran form. In Georgia it is found in the extreme southeast. princeps is sometimes treated at species rank as Novoeumeces princeps — the checklist keeps it as a subspecies. The figure is from Vashlovani National Park; barcodes are from Chachuna Managed Reserve. It is harmless to people.",
