    "description": "An introduced lacertid — a single Georgian locality (Anaklia), not native fauna.",
    "overview": "The Lebanon lizard (Phoenicolacerta laevis) is a lacertid. Tarkhnishvili et al. 2026 treat species status as biologically valid and list it as unintentionally introduced: a single location in Georgia, genetically close to populations from southern Türkiye. The Georgian record is Tarkhnishvili et al. (2017a); the discussion names it, with Trachemys scripta, as introduced from distant geographic regions (Tarkhnishvili et al. 2017b; Reshetnikov et al. 2023). Figure and barcodes are from Anaklia. It is harmless to people.",
